WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.692
Both methods are useful.

00:00:01.692 --> 00:00:06.502
UNION ALL is explicit and easy to read when there are only a few columns.

00:00:06.502 --> 00:00:11.787
LATERAL VALUES is compact when many columns follow the same repeated structure.

00:00:11.787 --> 00:00:16.812
The correct choice is the one that keeps the transformation clear and maintainable.

00:00:16.812 --> 00:00:20.777
Unpivoting turns repeated columns into row values.

00:00:20.777 --> 00:00:27.117
UNION ALL is explicit and portable; LATERAL VALUES can be more compact in PostgreSQL.

00:00:27.117 --> 00:00:33.997
The important design decision is which columns become identifiers and which column names become values.

00:00:33.997 --> 00:00:37.493
Keep data types compatible across the generated rows.
